# Architecture rules

Read `AGENTS.md` for the canonical shared rules. This file governs *where code goes*.

## Monorepo layout
- `apps/desktop/` — Electron shell (main/preload/renderer), secure IPC, spawns the Python sidecar.
- `apps/web-editor/` — React + TS editor UI (timeline, preview, panels).
- `packages/timeline-schema/` — `Project/Timeline/Track/Clip/Effect/Keyframe` schemas (Zod), versioning + migrations.
- `packages/shared-types/` — cross-package TS types only.
- `packages/editor-core/` — typed timeline operations + patch engine (apply/invert/validate/diff/undo).
- `packages/ai-sdk/` — AI orchestrator, tool registry, context builder, memory store.
- `packages/ui/` — shared React components.
- `engine/python/framepilot_engine/` — `render/ timeline/ effects/ audio/ tracking/ masking/ validation/ ai_tools/`.
- `tests/e2e/` — Playwright suite. `plan/PLAN.md` — build plan. `docs/` — all docs.

## Package boundaries (enforce)
- `editor-core` is the ONLY place timeline operations are applied. UI and AI call into it.
- `ai-sdk` depends on `editor-core` and `timeline-schema` — never reaches into the Python render engine to mutate state. It emits **patches**.
- `timeline-schema` has no runtime deps on other packages (it is the contract).
- `shared-types` holds types only — no logic.
- The Python render engine is **isolated** so the desktop shell (Electron now, possibly Tauri later) can change without touching it.

## Render engine vs preview engine (HARD RULE, PRD §9.2)
- **Render engine = Python MoviePy + FFmpeg.** Final export, preview *render*, waveforms, frame extraction, masks, tracking, proxies. Deterministic.
- **Preview engine = the UI.** HTML `<video>`, canvas/WebGL overlays, proxy/low-res media.
- ❌ Never call MoviePy for the real-time UI preview path.

## Where things go (examples)
- New timeline operation → `packages/editor-core` (+ schema in `timeline-schema`, + Python counterpart in `engine/.../timeline`).
- New AI tool → `packages/ai-sdk` tool registry (+ `engine/.../ai_tools` if it needs the engine). Returns a patch.
- New render/effect/codec logic → `engine/python/framepilot_engine/`.
- New UI panel → `apps/web-editor` (+ shared bits in `packages/ui`).
